  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — comparing the most favorable outcome in the least probable scenario — is not considered by the individual. In Lottery B, the least probable outcome is 0 Euros (worst), and in Lottery A, the only outcome is 2400 Euros (best). The reason would prefer A because 2400 > 0. The individual, however, focuses on the low probability of getting 0 Euros in B and sees that as a positive, which is not aligned with the rule of preferring the lottery with the more favorable least probable outcome. Instead, they are reasoning about the low chance of a bad outcome, which is not the same as evaluating the most favorable outcome at the lowest probability. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason as defined. The justification is inconsistent with the rule of the reason. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
